%erg v1
Title: Merge subsumed structural checks in test_new.sh
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-05T07:26Z claude created

--- body ---
`tests/test_new.sh` has individual tests for magic line, log separator, body separator,
Title, Author, and Created headers (lines 39–79). These are all subsumed by the
"generated file passes erg validate" test at line 33: if `erg validate` passes, all format
invariants are satisfied by definition.

The individual checks add line count and maintenance burden without adding diagnostic value
— a failure in "log separator present" means exactly the same thing as a failure in
"generated file passes erg validate".

Two options (choose one):
A) Drop the 6 redundant field-check tests, keep only the validate test. Rely on validate's
   error message for diagnosis.
B) Drop the validate test, keep the field checks. Gives precise per-field failure messages
   at the cost of not testing the format holistically.

Recommendation: option A. The validate test is the single source of truth; if validation
logic changes, only one place needs updating. Add a comment above the validate test
explaining it subsumes all structural checks.
